   "h0_reference": null,
   "fallback": null,
   "drift_bands_apply": false,
   "_basis": "reports/phase-9b.md section 3: raw validation ECE-22 better than the neural head in 16 of 16 windows (2.11x-8.35x, median 3.44x) and recalibrated evaluation ECE better in 12 of 16 (reports/phase-9a.md); cost is 0.88%-2.39% of exact CRPS, in which the head wins 16 of 16.",
   "_reversal_condition": "RE-OPEN THIS if guide 10.2's allocation optimiser becomes the consuming path. An optimiser consumes the whole distribution, so it pays the proper score, where the neural head wins 16 of 16; the calibration advantage that justified this switch is a marginal-probability property that matters when a planner reads P(fill complete) directly. See phase-9b.md B.5.",
